+# Pre-Ship Review — USDC Payouts dApp (Base)
+
+Reviewer pass on the frontend + config before end-of-week ship. Report only — no code changed.
+Scope: `packages/nextjs`. Most issues live in `app/payouts/page.tsx`.
+
+Severity legend: **ship-blocking** (users hit a broken/confusing/failing flow, or trust/security risk) · **should-fix** (quality/UX/reliability, not a hard blocker).
+
+---
+
+## Ship-blocking
+
+### 1. Wallet connection is TEXT, not a Connect button
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:70-71`
+- Disconnected users see `<p>Please connect your wallet to send a payout.</p>` — a dead end with no way to act.
+- **Fix:** Render the connect button as the primary UI:
+  ```tsx
+  import { RainbowKitCustomConnectButton } from "~~/components/scaffold-eth";
+  ...
+  {!isConnected ? <RainbowKitCustomConnectButton /> : ( ...form... )}
+  ```
+
+### 2. Uses raw wagmi `useWriteContract` instead of `useScaffoldWriteContract`
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:6,21`
+- `useWriteContract().isPending` flips back to `false` when the wallet returns the tx **hash**, not when the tx **confirms** on-chain. So `isPending`-gated buttons re-enable mid-flight → duplicate approvals/payouts. Also loses SE-2's built-in tx notifications/block-confirmation waiting.
+- **Fix:** Use `useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "Payouts" })` and a second instance for `USDC`. Call `writeContractAsync({ functionName, args })` (no manual address/abi needed once contracts are registered — see #5).
+
+### 3. Approve + Send shown together; no per-action lock → double-submit
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+- Both buttons are always visible and both gated by the same single `isPending`. There is no `approvalSubmitting` (click→hash gap) or `approveCooldown` (confirm→cache-refresh gap), and no allowance check to hide Approve once allowance is sufficient. Users can double-approve or click Send before approval confirms → failing txs.
+- **Fix:** One primary CTA at a time. Read allowance via `useScaffoldReadContract` USDC `allowance(owner, Payouts)`; if `allowance < amount` show **Approve**, else show **Send Payout**. Lock the button with two states both on `disabled`:
+  ```tsx
+  disabled={isPending || approvalSubmitting || approveCooldown}
+  ```
+  Set `approvalSubmitting` at handler top, clear in `finally`; set `approveCooldown` after the await, clear after ~4s + `refetchAllowance()`.
+
+### 4. No wrong-network handling in the CTA slot
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx` (entire action area; target chain is Base `8453`)
+- If a connected wallet is on the wrong chain, the code calls `pay`/`approve` anyway and eats a silent wagmi error. The header `WrongNetworkDropdown` is not enough.
+- **Fix:** Branch the primary button on `useChainId() === base.id`; on mismatch render a `useSwitchChain`-driven **"Switch to Base"** button in the same slot.
+
+### 5. External USDC contract hand-added to the AUTOGENERATED `deployedContracts.ts`
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:50` (USDC block); `externalContracts.ts` is empty (`{}`)
+- `deployedContracts.ts` header literally says "autogenerated ... you should not edit it manually or your changes might be overwritten." The next `yarn deploy` regenerates the file and wipes the USDC entry. Because `page.tsx:11` reads `deployedContracts[8453].USDC` at **module scope**, that turns into a build/runtime crash of the whole page, not a soft failure.
+- **Fix:** Move the USDC address+ABI to `packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts`:
+  ```ts
+  const externalContracts = {
+    8453: { USDC: { address: "0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913", abi: [...] } },
+  } as const;
+  ```
+  Then reference it via `useScaffoldReadContract`/`useScaffoldWriteContract` with `contractName: "USDC"` (both files feed the same hook registry).
+
+### 6. Contract verification on Basescan — must confirm
+- **Addresses:** Payouts `0x7c3f2A9d41B85E60Cf14a14e2b9D073A55e0b6F2`, USDC `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913` (canonical Base USDC — already verified).
+- Could not programmatically confirm the **Payouts** contract's verification (explorer page is JS-rendered). Verify manually before ship: open the Payouts address on basescan.org and confirm the green "Contract Source Code Verified" check. Unverified = trust red flag.
+- **Fix if unverified:** `yarn verify --network base`.
+
+### 7. SE-2 default branding still in place
+- **Tab title:** `app/layout.tsx:11` → `title: 'Scaffold-ETH 2 App'`, and `utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts:8` → `titleTemplate = "%s | Scaffold-ETH 2"`. Every tab reads "… | Scaffold-ETH 2". **Fix:** set app name (e.g. `title: 'USDC Payouts'`, template `"%s | USDC Payouts"`).
+- **Footer:** `components/Footer.tsx:50-74` — "Fork me" → SE-2 repo, "Built with ❤ at BuidlGuidl", "Support" Telegram. **Fix:** replace with the project's own repo/support links or remove.
+- **README:** repo root README is the stock Scaffold-ETH 2 template. **Fix:** replace with a README describing the Payouts dApp.
+- **Favicon:** `public/favicon.png` — confirm it is not the SE-2 default diamond; replace if so.
+
+---
+
+## Should-fix
+
+### 8. Hardcoded dark background bypasses the DaisyUI theme
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:65` (`bg-black text-white`), also `:121` (`border-gray-700`).
+- Light-mode users get a black page and the header theme toggle does nothing on this page.
+- **Fix:** `bg-base-200 text-base-content`; use `border-base-300` for the list rows. (Or force `data-theme="dark"` on `<html>` and remove `<SwitchTheme/>` — but semantic classes are the cleaner fix.)
+
+### 9. Recipient uses a raw `<input type="text">` instead of `<AddressInput/>`
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:78-84`
+- No ENS resolution, no validation, no blockie preview. Line 55 then casts `recipient as \`0x${string}\`` and sends whatever string was typed — a typo'd/invalid address sends the payout into the void.
+- **Fix:** `<AddressInput value={recipient} onChange={setRecipient} placeholder="0x... or ENS name" />` from `@scaffold-ui/components`, and disable Send until it resolves to a valid address.
+
+### 10. Payouts contract address never shown on the page
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx`
+- Users can't see which contract they're approving/paying. **Fix:** show `<Address address={PAYOUTS.address} />` near the header.
+
+### 11. No USD value next to USDC amounts
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:75` (balance), `:126` (history rows), amount input.
+- USDC ≈ $1 so this is low-stakes, but the checklist wants a dollar figure alongside token amounts. **Fix:** render `(~$X)` next to balance and each payout amount.
+
+### 12. Errors are swallowed — no user feedback
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:44-46,59-61`
+- `catch (e) { console.error(e) }` — a failed approve/pay looks like nothing happened. No raw-error → readable-message mapping.
+- **Fix:** `notification.error(getParsedError(e))` from `~~/utils/scaffold-eth`. (Switching to `useScaffoldWriteContract` per #2 also gives success/error toasts for free.)
+
+### 13. `pollingInterval` is the 30s default
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:24` → `pollingInterval: 30000`
+- Base is an L2; 30s makes balances/history feel frozen. **Fix:** `3000`.
+
+### 14. RPC: default Alchemy key + bare `http()` fallback
+- **Files:** `scaffold.config.ts:29` (falls back to shipped `DEFAULT_ALCHEMY_API_KEY`), `:32-35` (`rpcOverrides` empty); `services/web3/wagmiConfig.tsx:20` includes a bare `http()` transport in the fallback list.
+- In production this silently hits rate-limited public RPC. **Fix:** set `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` on Vercel (confirm with `vercel env ls`), add a Base `rpcOverrides` entry, and drop the bare `http()` fallback so only intended transports remain.
+
+### 15. Button `loading` class antipattern
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:101,108` → ``className={`btn ... ${isPending ? "loading" : ""}`}``
+- DaisyUI's `loading` class on a `btn` replaces the whole label with a full-size spinner (looks broken). **Fix:** drop `loading` from the class; put an inline `<span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm mr-2" />` inside the button next to the text.
+
+### 16. Pill-shaped inputs — `--radius-field: 9999rem`
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/styles/globals.css:36,63` (both light and dark theme blocks)
+- The recipient/amount inputs and the memo textarea render as pills and clip content. **Fix:** set `--radius-field: 0.5rem` in both blocks (theme-level, not per-component).
+
+### 17. Phantom wallet missing from RainbowKit list
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:20-28`
+- List is metaMask/walletConnect/ledger/baseAccount/rainbow/safe. Many Base users use Phantom and can't connect. **Fix:** add `phantomWallet` to the `wallets` array.
+
+### 18. No mobile wallet deep-linking
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx` (write handlers)
+- On mobile WalletConnect the wallet app doesn't auto-open after a tx request, so approve/pay appear to hang. **Fix:** wrap each write in a `writeAndOpen` helper — fire the write first, then `setTimeout(openWallet, 2000)`; detect the wallet from WC session data (not just `connector.id`); skip when `window.ethereum` exists (in-app browser).
+
+---
+
+## Notes / passed
+- OG image (`getMetadata.ts:19,34`) builds an **absolute** URL from `metadataBase`/`VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL` — OK in production, but confirm `VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL` is set so it doesn't fall back to `localhost:3000` in unfurls.
+- Event history uses `fromBlock: 0n` (`page.tsx:32`). The contract has `deployedOnBlock: 33712450` — scanning from 0 on Base mainnet is a large, slow range and may hit RPC log-range limits. Consider `fromBlock: 33712450n`.
+- Payout list `key={i}` (`page.tsx:120`) — prefer a stable key (tx hash + log index) to avoid re-render glitches with `watch: true`.

